  "9001": {
   "feedTitle": "The Coastal Courier",
   "title": "Town votes to bring the old tide mill back to life",
   "author": "Hannah Ellery",
   "url": "https://example.org/9001",
   "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T21:15:00Z",
   "summary": "The harbour authority voted on Tuesday night to rebuild the old tide mill as a working museum, ending a twelve-year argument about what to do with the most photographed ruin on the coast.",
   "imageUrl": "https://example.org/img/lead.jpg",
   "wordCount": 980,
   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": {
      "text": "The harbour authority voted on Tuesday night to rebuild the old tide mill as a working museum, ending a twelve-year argument about what to do with the most photographed ruin on the coast.",
      "spans": []
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": {
      "text": "The vote was nine to four. Supporters packed the public gallery and applauded when the chair read the result; the four councillors who voted against said the town could not afford the running costs once the grant money is spent.",
      "spans": []
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": {
      "text": "Work will start in the spring. The plan restores the wheel, the sluice gates and the miller’s house, and adds a small café in the grain store. On the highest tides of the year the wheel will turn again, grinding flour that the café will bake into bread.",
      "spans": [
       {
        "start": 150,
        "end": 163,
        "style": "i"
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "h",
     "level": 2,
     "text": {
      "text": "A building that refused to fall down",
      "spans": []
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": {
      "text": "The mill was built in 1793 and worked until 1938, when a storm broke the sea wall and flooded the wheel pit. It has stood roofless since the 1950s. Three earlier schemes, a hotel, flats and a sailing school, all stalled when their backers found out what it costs to work on a listed building that the sea visits twice a day.",
      "spans": []
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "quote",
     "paragraphs": [
      {
       "text": "People think a ruin is free. It is the most expensive thing a town can own, because every winter it asks you again what you are going to do about it.",
       "spans": []
      }
     ],
     "citation": {
      "text": "Mairead Quinn, chair of the harbour authority",
      "spans": []
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": {
      "text": "Engineers surveyed the structure last year and found it in better shape than anyone expected. The walls are sound to the first floor; the timber is gone, but the oak beams that carried the floors left sockets that show exactly where each one went.",
      "spans": []
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "img",
     "url": "https://example.org/img/mill-plan.png",
     "caption": {
      "text": "The restored mill as the architects drew it, seen from the harbour wall.",
      "spans": []
     },
     "width": 1200,
     "height": 800
    },
    {
     "t": "h",
     "level": 3,
     "text": {
      "text": "What the money buys",
      "spans": []
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "list",
     "ordered": false,
     "items": [
      {
       "text": "A new roof in Welsh slate, on oak trusses made to the old pattern",
       "spans": []
      },
      {
       "text": "The wheel rebuilt from the surviving iron hub, with new elm paddles",
       "spans": []
      },
      {
       "text": "Sluice gates that can be closed in a storm surge, protecting the quay as well as the mill",
       "spans": []
      },
      {
       "text": "A ground-floor gallery that stays open all year, free to enter",
       "spans": []
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": {
      "text": "The grant from the national heritage fund covers £2.4 million of the £3.1 million cost. The rest is to come from a public appeal, which opened yesterday and had raised £41,000 by the evening.",
      "spans": []
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": {
      "text": "Opponents say the appeal is optimistic. “We have been here before,” said Councillor Peter Hale, who voted against. “Everyone loves the mill on a postcard. Fewer people love it on a spreadsheet.”",
      "spans": []
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "pre",
     "text": "Tide   Height  Wheel\n06:12  5.8 m   turns\n18:40  6.1 m   turns\n07:01  4.2 m   idle",
     "language": null
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": {
      "text": "The museum is due to open in the summer of 2028. Until then the harbour wall will stay open to walkers, and the authority promises a viewing platform so that people can watch the work.",
      "spans": []
     }
    },
    {
     "t": "video",
     "src": "unknown block type, skipped"
    }
   ],
